  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The current implementation of fcrepo-camel allows a user to interact with a remote fedora repository over https by setting the secure=true URI parameter.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I do not think this is a good implementation. It is error prone and departs from how this is handled in other camel components (such as http4).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The better implementation would remove the 'secure' option and instead use the https:// protocol if the fedora port is set as 443 (otherwise using ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://)/"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": ". I am not convinced that there is a use case for using https:// with non-standard ports (e.g. 9443), and as it stands, this seems like an unnecessary option.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If that use case emerges, we can revisit this decision.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
